I look at the recipe on my phone again.
I need to make food for three people today.
First, I take a piece of paper and a pen.
I read the list of ingredients.
Then, I check the spice shelf in the kitchen.
There is enough turmeric powder and chili powder here.
But there is no coriander powder.
After that, I write coriander powder on the paper.
We need chicken for the curry.
For three people, half a kilo of chicken is enough.
I write that down too.
Next, I check the vegetables.
I need exactly two big onions and three tomatoes.
I add them to the list.
I also need some ginger and green chilies.
Now the shopping list is ready.
I take my umbrella and cloth bag.
I set out to the market.
